<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cinco Villas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cinco Villas is a comarca in the north-west of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> in Aragon, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, named after five towns raised to the rank of villa by Philip V in the early 18th century. In antiquity the area was home to the Suessetani, and it contains Roman remains such as the town of Los Bañales. Its main town is Ejea de los Caballeros.</p></div>
